    <field name="NAME">announcePlotter</field>
    <statement name="STACK">
      <block type="serial_text">
        <field name="TEXT">@plot {"version":1,"id":"pot-dashboard","title":"Turn the potentiometer","history":200,"fields":[{"id":"adc","label":"ADC","min":0,"max":1023},{"id":"volts","label":"Voltage","unit":"V","min":0,"max":5,"derive":{"op":"formula","expr":"adc * 5 / 1023"}}],"widgets":[{"type":"gauge","field":"volts"},{"type":"bar","field":"adc"},{"type":"line","fields":["adc"]},{"type":"raw","fields":["adc","volts"]}],"description":"Potentiometer dashboard: A0 wiper, outer legs GND/VCC. Send one ADC number; Plotter computes volts assuming 5 V ADC reference. Change the formula for a different measured reference."}</field>
        <field name="END">println</field>
        <comment pinned="false" w="390" h="170">This is an ordinary Serial text message stored in Flash. Click it to edit formatted JSON. The computer creates instruments and computes derived fields; this sketch sends only input values.</comment>
        <next>
          <block type="serial_text">
            <field name="TEXT">@msg Potentiometer dashboard: A0 wiper, outer legs GND/VCC. Send one ADC number; Plotter computes volts assuming 5 V ADC reference. Change the formula for a different measured reference. Press Start to begin; Stop pauses readings.</field>
            <field name="END">println</field>
          </block>
        </next>
      </block>
    </statement>
    <comment pinned="false" w="390" h="170">Send this one header from setup and again after Start. It describes the views and gives the next action. Edit this text block to change the dashboard; data order must match fields.</comment>
